  "id": "descending-tract",
  "term": "descending tract",
  "definition": "A descending tract is a neural pathway referred to in studies of walking, where a lesion to it can impair walking and recovery depends on neuroplastic changes. In this context, it is linked to corticomotor drive during movement.",
